{"name":"Swedish Clover","hex":"#7b8867","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clover","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the genus Trifolium with leaves usually divided into three (rarely four) leaflets and with white or red flowers.","The second Lenormand card, representing hope, optimism and short-term luck."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clover"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clover","blocks":[{"text":"Clovers, also called trefoils, are plants of the genus Trifolium. They are herbaceous plants growing up to 30 cm (12 in) tall. The leaves are usually trifoliate and the small flowers are reddish to white or yellow. Related genera with similar common names include Melilotus and Medicago (burclover)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/79_Trifolium_repens_L.jpg/330px-79_Trifolium_repens_L.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clover"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Trifolium_dubium_RF.jpg/250px-Trifolium_dubium_RF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Trifolium_dubium_RF.jpg/500px-Trifolium_dubium_RF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Trifolium_dubium_RF.jpg/250px-Trifolium_dubium_RF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATrifolium_dubium_RF.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Trifolium_alpestre_RF.jpg/330px-Trifolium_alpestre_RF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Trifolium_alpestre_RF.jpg/960px-Trifolium_alpestre_RF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip